      "title": "Session Controller: Resolving Unexpected Logouts and Elevated Privileges via Certificate and Access Reviews",
      "content_summary": "Troubleshoot unexpected logouts, elevated privilege alerts, and account lockouts in Session Controller by inspecting expired certificates and completing improper access reviews.",
      "content_body": "When users report unexpected logouts or account lockouts, first check the Session Controller logs for certificate validation failures. Expired user or server certificates often trigger forced session terminations and privilege escalation warnings. Renew any expired certificates immediately and verify the new chain of trust. If issues persist, audit recent permission changes to ensure no improper access grants remain active. Complete a formal access review to reconcile user roles with current security policies. Confirm that all flagged privileges are revoked or updated to the correct baseline."
